WEBVTT

00:00:26.156 --> 00:00:27.592
&lt;i&gt;First officer's log,&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:27.635 --> 00:00:29.985
&lt;i&gt;stardate 58499.2.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.510
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Cerritos &lt;i&gt;is in for repairs
at Douglas Station&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:32.553 --> 00:00:34.555
&lt;i&gt;after a pounding from the Breen.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:34.599 --> 00:00:36.296
We took an even harder pounding

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:37.558
&lt;i&gt;in the media
after one of the new&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:37.602 --> 00:00:39.865
Texas-class ships
had to swoop in

00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:41.997
and save us our asses.

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.521
&lt;i&gt;Captain Freeman's
been called back&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:43.564 --> 00:00:45.740
&lt;i&gt;to Starfleet Command
for questioning.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:45.784 --> 00:00:47.220
&lt;i&gt;Disappointment is&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:47.264 --> 00:00:48.569
&lt;i&gt;an understatement,
Captain Freeman.&lt;/i&gt;

00:00:48.613 --> 00:00:50.919
Project Swing By
was a waste of resources,

00:00:50.963 --> 00:00:53.183
and you almost got
your crew killed.

00:00:53.226 --> 00:00:55.185
We did uncover
a Breen insurgency.

00:00:55.228 --> 00:00:57.404
An attack you could've been
prepared for

00:00:57.448 --> 00:01:00.146
if the culture on your ship
was more professional.

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:01.974
Admiral, I assure you,

00:01:02.017 --> 00:01:04.411
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew
takes their duty seriously.

00:01:04.455 --> 00:01:06.152
Captain Freeman's right.

00:01:06.196 --> 00:01:08.502
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is a necessary part
of the fleet.

00:01:08.546 --> 00:01:11.462
However, my automated
Texas-class ships

00:01:11.505 --> 00:01:14.639
are her superior,
with zero human error.

00:01:14.682 --> 00:01:16.336
They haven't even been tested.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.947
I recommend decommissioning
the California-class

00:01:18.991 --> 00:01:21.472
and let the Texas-class
handle second contact.

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:24.170
Starfleet was founded
as a way for humanity

00:01:24.214 --> 00:01:25.693
to advance into the stars.

00:01:25.737 --> 00:01:27.869
This would undo
centuries of progress.

00:01:27.913 --> 00:01:30.220
Captain, I'm sorry,
but there are plenty of other

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:32.091
crewed ships in the fleet.

00:01:32.135 --> 00:01:34.485
The council has decided to take
Admiral Buenamigo's advice

00:01:34.528 --> 00:01:37.357
and shutter
the California-class.

00:02:46.948 --> 00:02:48.776
Come on, Les.

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.779
You know that AI can't navigate
complex problems like I can.

00:02:51.823 --> 00:02:53.651
The Texas-class will save lives.

00:02:53.694 --> 00:02:55.653
The California-class
already does.

00:02:55.696 --> 00:02:57.785
I'm fighting this,
and I don't want my crew

00:02:57.829 --> 00:02:59.787
hearing anything
until I've had my say.

00:02:59.831 --> 00:03:01.615
&lt;i&gt;Guys! Guys!&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:01.659 --> 00:03:03.313
&lt;i&gt;Hans just told me that
the Phylosian in Tactical's&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:03.356 --> 00:03:05.358
girlfriend's Vedek
heard that Starfleet Command

00:03:05.402 --> 00:03:07.578
is shuttering the Cali-class
and replacing it with drones!

00:03:07.621 --> 00:03:09.275
Who's Hans?

00:03:09.319 --> 00:03:11.495
- You know, towel guy.
- The gossip king?

00:03:11.538 --> 00:03:13.366
He's never been wrong.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.455
We're all gonna get reassigned.
I can't work at an outpost.

00:03:15.499 --> 00:03:17.370
I won't look good
in a drab olive vest.

00:03:17.414 --> 00:03:19.067
Does that mean I'm not gonna
be able to keep doing

00:03:19.111 --> 00:03:20.721
senior science officer training?

00:03:20.765 --> 00:03:23.202
When some computer's
doing our jobs? Probably not.

00:03:23.246 --> 00:03:25.944
Whoa. These Texas-class ships
are amazing.

00:03:25.987 --> 00:03:27.206
Rutherford, stop being impressed
with the thing

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.294
that's stealing our jobs.

00:03:28.338 --> 00:03:29.991
Sorry, sorry. No. I don't know

00:03:30.035 --> 00:03:31.471
what I would do without
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt; but...

00:03:31.515 --> 00:03:32.907
Ooh, baby, look at this code.

00:03:32.951 --> 00:03:34.692
At least someone found
a silver lining.

00:03:34.735 --> 00:03:37.564
Oh, man, I wonder how
the bridge crew's taking it.

00:03:37.608 --> 00:03:39.087
Dr. T'Ana's probably like,

00:03:39.131 --> 00:03:40.524
:
"Holy [bleep] [bleep].

00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:41.612
I'm a doctor,
not an [bleep]hole."

00:03:41.655 --> 00:03:43.309
Ooh, ooh, do Ransom.

00:03:43.353 --> 00:03:45.920
:
"If I can't have my private gym,

00:03:45.964 --> 00:03:47.748
I might move back to Barcelona."

00:03:47.792 --> 00:03:49.533
- Barcelona.
- Okay, okay.

00:03:49.576 --> 00:03:50.925
Wait, wait, wait, who's this?

00:03:50.969 --> 00:03:52.187
:
"Hey, baby bear.

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:53.580
"The only thing I'll miss

00:03:53.624 --> 00:03:55.321
"is being able
to eject the warp core.

00:03:55.365 --> 00:03:57.497
"I talk about prophets

00:03:57.541 --> 00:03:58.498
even more than a Ferengi."

00:03:58.542 --> 00:03:59.760
Is that what

00:03:59.804 --> 00:04:00.935
I sound like to you?

00:04:00.979 --> 00:04:01.849
:
Lieutenant Shaxs.

00:04:01.893 --> 00:04:02.763
No. I-I didn't mean...

00:04:02.807 --> 00:04:03.634
I was going to ask you

00:04:03.677 --> 00:04:05.070
for help with my phaser,

00:04:05.113 --> 00:04:07.551
but I guess I'm just
a big joke to you!

00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:10.684
Wait. I'm sorry! Ah.

00:04:10.728 --> 00:04:11.816
I can't leave
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; knowing

00:04:11.859 --> 00:04:13.383
a senior officer hates me.

00:04:14.645 --> 00:04:16.342
The longer Mariner's not around,

00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:18.431
the more Boimler kind of
loses his grasp on reality.

00:04:18.475 --> 00:04:20.303
I still feel awful
about how we acted

00:04:20.346 --> 00:04:21.739
when she got transferred.

00:04:21.782 --> 00:04:23.393
Yeah, we should've been
more supportive.

00:04:23.436 --> 00:04:26.396
I hope she's okay,
all alone out in space.

00:04:26.439 --> 00:04:27.919
She's probably miserable.

00:04:27.962 --> 00:04:29.050
&lt;i&gt;All right!&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:30.574 --> 00:04:32.750
Damn you, Starfleet!

00:04:32.793 --> 00:04:34.752
Ha!

00:04:34.795 --> 00:04:37.276
Well, nice try,
but I'm not Starfleet.

00:04:38.408 --> 00:04:40.323
You're still a filthy "hew-mon."

00:04:40.366 --> 00:04:41.498
You got me there.

00:04:41.541 --> 00:04:43.238
Hey, I got the idol.

00:04:43.282 --> 00:04:44.631
&lt;i&gt;PETRA [over comms]:
And you're sneaking out&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:44.675 --> 00:04:46.067
&lt;i&gt;without making
a big deal of it, right?&lt;/i&gt;

00:04:46.111 --> 00:04:48.113
Oh, totally.
I'm playing it very cool.

00:04:48.156 --> 00:04:51.246
Better luck next time,
you dumb grave robbers.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:52.552
Okay, Petra, time to go.

00:04:52.596 --> 00:04:53.814
Beaming would be good.

00:04:53.858 --> 00:04:55.642
Anytime now, please.

00:05:03.433 --> 00:05:05.260
Having a little fun
down there, were we?

00:05:05.304 --> 00:05:07.132
You gonna send me to the brig?

00:05:07.175 --> 00:05:10.091
I don't care what you do, as
long as we can get this bad boy

00:05:10.135 --> 00:05:12.006
to the Qualor Historical Museum.

00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.834
Ooh, and our route takes us

00:05:13.878 --> 00:05:15.923
right through
the Bitrus Expanse.

00:05:15.967 --> 00:05:17.751
Want to excavate
a couple temples on the way?

00:05:17.795 --> 00:05:19.797
Yeah, I do.
The more hidden the better.

00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:26.891
Rescuing artifacts from
black market thieves is great,

00:05:26.934 --> 00:05:28.501
but, you know,
the best part of this gig

00:05:28.545 --> 00:05:30.198
is that you never get
pissed off.

00:05:30.242 --> 00:05:31.809
Thanks for letting me
do my thing.

00:05:31.852 --> 00:05:33.332
Yeah, well, with our funding,
we'll both be able

00:05:33.376 --> 00:05:35.247
to do our thing
for as long as we want.

00:05:35.290 --> 00:05:37.380
Oh, yeah, who's footing the bill
for all this?

00:05:37.423 --> 00:05:38.685
It has to cost, like, a fortune.

00:05:38.729 --> 00:05:40.426
Aw, that's cute,

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.472
pretending you have any concept
of how money works.

00:05:42.515 --> 00:05:44.169
But we donate everything
to museums,

00:05:44.212 --> 00:05:46.432
so how do we pay
for our fuel and gear?

00:05:46.476 --> 00:05:47.477
How'd you get this ship?

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:49.000
I'll handle the finances,

00:05:49.043 --> 00:05:50.697
and you worry about grabbing us

00:05:50.741 --> 00:05:53.657
some frosty Rom-Ales
for the warp.

00:05:54.658 --> 00:05:55.920
Hmm.

00:05:56.877 --> 00:05:59.227
&lt;i&gt;It's understandable&lt;/i&gt;

00:05:59.271 --> 00:06:01.578
that the captain isn't keen
on losing her command,

00:06:01.621 --> 00:06:04.363
which is why I would like
to offer her a promotion:

00:06:04.407 --> 00:06:07.148
fleet captain
of the entire Texas-class.

00:06:07.192 --> 00:06:09.629
I don't want
some operations desk job.

00:06:09.673 --> 00:06:11.849
Ah, wait till you see
the uniform.

00:06:11.892 --> 00:06:14.199
It has four epaulettes.

00:06:14.242 --> 00:06:16.375
This is his vanity project,
not mine.

00:06:16.419 --> 00:06:19.247
His ships do seem superior
to the Cali-class.

00:06:19.291 --> 00:06:21.336
Well, then he should prove it.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.991
I challenge you
to a mission race.

00:06:24.035 --> 00:06:26.385
If your drones really are
better than my crew,

00:06:26.429 --> 00:06:28.082
then it should be easy.

00:06:28.126 --> 00:06:31.259
Captain Freeman is begging
to prove her obsolescence.

00:06:31.303 --> 00:06:32.696
You can't allow her

00:06:32.739 --> 00:06:34.524
- to humiliate her crew.
- Sorry,

00:06:34.567 --> 00:06:37.744
I didn't know Buenamigo
was in charge here.

00:06:37.788 --> 00:06:40.704
Oh, please. These fine admirals
know that I am right,

00:06:40.747 --> 00:06:43.402
but if this is what you want...

00:06:46.013 --> 00:06:47.537
&lt;i&gt;We're doing what?!&lt;/i&gt;

00:06:47.580 --> 00:06:49.147
A second contact race.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:51.497
- What even is that?
- I made it up on the spot.

00:06:51.541 --> 00:06:54.152
A multi-planet mission,
timed and judged.

00:06:54.195 --> 00:06:56.763
Repairs,
outpost install, resupply.

00:06:56.807 --> 00:06:58.548
We could do these in our sleep.

00:06:58.591 --> 00:07:00.985
Exactly, and it'll be
the first time for the &lt;i&gt;Aledo.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:01.028 --> 00:07:02.769
That gives us an edge.

00:07:02.813 --> 00:07:04.423
Make sure your departments know

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:06.251
we're not just fighting
for ourselves.

00:07:06.294 --> 00:07:09.646
We have to do this
for the entire California-class.

00:07:09.689 --> 00:07:12.039
Let's see some hustle, people.

00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:14.259
We're doing Galaxy-class
engineering today.

00:07:14.302 --> 00:07:15.739
Do you hear me, Mr. Rutherford?

00:07:15.782 --> 00:07:17.218
Sorry, sir. Yes, sir.

00:07:17.262 --> 00:07:19.656
I want to see Commander
Data-level work, people.

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:21.919
Those isolinear chips
better be a blur.

00:07:21.962 --> 00:07:23.268
T'ANA:
Let's go, let's go!

00:07:23.311 --> 00:07:24.965
I didn't spend
seven [bleep] years

00:07:25.009 --> 00:07:27.272
on a goddamn Oberth
to get knocked down

00:07:27.315 --> 00:07:28.752
to station physician.

00:07:28.795 --> 00:07:30.144
All this work to become
a senior science officer.

00:07:30.188 --> 00:07:32.059
Now there might not be
any officers.

00:07:32.103 --> 00:07:33.974
Tendi, that's cantaloupe talk.

00:07:34.018 --> 00:07:36.107
I want to you to be
a can-aloupe.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:37.761
Remember your training,
and you'll do great.

00:07:37.804 --> 00:07:40.285
Thanks, Dr. Migleemo.
At first, I was worried...

00:07:41.504 --> 00:07:42.809
What are you doing here?!

00:07:42.853 --> 00:07:44.028
Get the [bleep] out
of my sick bay!

00:07:44.071 --> 00:07:45.682
You need to sit?

00:07:45.725 --> 00:07:47.553
Cross your leg over
the back of it and slam down.

00:07:47.597 --> 00:07:48.946
Command that chair.

00:07:50.556 --> 00:07:53.298
Sir, please, I respect you
and all Bajorans.

00:07:53.341 --> 00:07:55.082
Oh, so all Bajorans
are the same?

00:07:55.126 --> 00:07:56.214
What? No, no, I didn't mean...

00:07:56.257 --> 00:07:57.607
Get away from me!

00:07:57.650 --> 00:07:58.521
I need to concentrate
on the mission.

00:08:03.308 --> 00:08:04.875
We're in position, Captain.

00:08:08.748 --> 00:08:11.534
&lt;i&gt;I should thank you
for doing this, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:11.577 --> 00:08:13.492
&lt;i&gt;It's the perfect way
for me to show off&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:13.536 --> 00:08:15.059
&lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Aledo's &lt;i&gt;capabilities.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:15.102 --> 00:08:17.322
Not a problem at all, Admiral.

00:08:17.365 --> 00:08:20.455
Can't wait to see you fall
on that smug face.

00:08:20.499 --> 00:08:24.068
&lt;i&gt;Aledo,&lt;/i&gt; I'm uploading
mission parameters now.

00:08:24.111 --> 00:08:26.157
&lt;i&gt;Orders received.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:29.029
&lt;i&gt;On my mark, you may proceed.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:30.988 --> 00:08:33.425
- Mark.
- Warp me!

00:08:35.775 --> 00:08:38.169
&lt;i&gt;Shall I commence, Admiral?&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:38.212 --> 00:08:39.866
Negative, &lt;i&gt;Aledo.&lt;/i&gt;

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:42.477
Let's make this interesting,
give them a head start.

00:08:47.134 --> 00:08:49.702
On behalf of all Galardonians,
I want to thank...

00:08:49.746 --> 00:08:51.835
Yeah, no problem. Alpha, Beta:
install the rigging.

00:08:51.878 --> 00:08:53.706
Gamma, Epsilon: replace
the old system with the updated

00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:55.708
distribution nodes. Go, go, go!

00:09:01.018 --> 00:09:03.629
Rutherford, toss me
the scanner that looks like

00:09:03.673 --> 00:09:05.283
a phase discriminator.

00:09:05.326 --> 00:09:06.501
I know I've seen
this code before.

00:09:06.545 --> 00:09:07.590
Rutherford!

00:09:07.633 --> 00:09:09.548
Sorry. Here you go.

00:09:09.592 --> 00:09:11.245
Done.

00:09:11.289 --> 00:09:12.333
Whoa!

00:09:14.684 --> 00:09:17.730
Captain, half a power plant
just beamed in beside us.

00:09:17.774 --> 00:09:20.428
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; can transport
prefabricated modules?

00:09:20.472 --> 00:09:21.865
We have to move!

00:09:21.908 --> 00:09:24.737
Billups to &lt;i&gt;Cerritos,&lt;/i&gt;
six to beam up.

00:09:31.091 --> 00:09:33.093
&lt;i&gt;We've arrived
at LT-358, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:33.137 --> 00:09:34.617
Scans indicate
the probe was right:

00:09:34.660 --> 00:09:36.488
- no signs of life.
- We're in the lead.

00:09:36.531 --> 00:09:39.622
Let's keep it that way, people.
Begin outpost installation.

00:09:49.066 --> 00:09:51.285
Huh.

00:09:57.727 --> 00:09:59.380
Let's go, people.
We got to wrap this up.

00:09:59.424 --> 00:10:01.600
Sir, I'm sorry, but
we have to stop construction.

00:10:01.644 --> 00:10:03.341
- What are you talking about?
- The scans missed

00:10:03.384 --> 00:10:05.299
microscopic signs of life
in the soil.

00:10:05.343 --> 00:10:07.345
We need to make sure
it isn't sentient.

00:10:07.388 --> 00:10:08.520
Everyone, stop!

00:10:08.563 --> 00:10:09.695
Captain, we have a potential

00:10:09.739 --> 00:10:11.131
microbial life down here.

00:10:11.175 --> 00:10:12.916
&lt;i&gt;We need to do
a full self-awareness assessment&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:12.959 --> 00:10:14.439
&lt;i&gt;before we finish the outpost.&lt;/i&gt;

00:10:14.482 --> 00:10:15.658
Wha-- [scoffs] Of course.

00:10:15.701 --> 00:10:17.572
But hurry.
We've just lost our lead.

00:10:20.314 --> 00:10:22.142
We're good.

00:10:22.186 --> 00:10:23.709
Okay, go, go, go!

00:10:23.753 --> 00:10:25.058
- Move, people! Let's go!
- I'm sorry.

00:10:25.102 --> 00:10:26.538
I-I could've sworn
there was life...

00:10:26.581 --> 00:10:28.192
No, no, no, this stuff
has a multiphasic charge,

00:10:28.235 --> 00:10:30.934
confuses the
out of a tricorder. Let's go.

00:10:30.977 --> 00:10:33.719
Outpost is complete, Captain.

00:10:33.763 --> 00:10:35.242
I need warp now!

00:10:37.201 --> 00:10:39.464
We just have to deliver
supplies to Ockmenic 9.

00:10:39.507 --> 00:10:42.423
It's one of those Brigadoon-type
planets that only phases

00:10:42.467 --> 00:10:44.469
into our dimension
for a couple hours a year.

00:10:44.512 --> 00:10:48.255
Hopefully, we can catch up
to the &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; before it appears.

00:10:55.306 --> 00:10:57.961
Ugh, this blows!
It's taking forever.

00:10:58.004 --> 00:10:59.919
Just don't embarrass me, okay?

00:10:59.963 --> 00:11:01.747
You're the one who begged
to come with me, all right?

00:11:01.791 --> 00:11:03.575
Well, I wanted to see the ship.

00:11:03.618 --> 00:11:05.446
They're gonna be in orbit.

00:11:05.490 --> 00:11:07.187
It's gonna be like
a tiny little dot.

00:11:07.231 --> 00:11:09.146
You're not going to
see them at all.

00:11:13.367 --> 00:11:16.588
Whoa, ho, ho, ho, ho. Hey!

00:11:16.631 --> 00:11:18.590
- Down here!
- They can't hear you.

00:11:18.633 --> 00:11:20.200
Thanks for all the stuff!

00:11:20.244 --> 00:11:21.593
All right, shut up
for a second.

00:11:21.636 --> 00:11:23.943
Supplies received.
The Ockmenians appreciate

00:11:23.987 --> 00:11:26.337
- all Starfleet...
- Next time, send a replicator!

00:11:26.380 --> 00:11:28.556
Oh, my God,
why are you like this?

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:31.472
&lt;i&gt;Captain, the planet
is already phasing away.&lt;/i&gt;

00:11:31.516 --> 00:11:34.780
No. No!

00:11:34.824 --> 00:11:37.130
We're too late.

00:11:53.103 --> 00:11:56.149
God, we would've won
if I hadn't defended the life

00:11:56.193 --> 00:11:57.629
of some inert dust.

00:11:57.672 --> 00:11:59.457
When secondary scans find life,

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.198
you have to drop everything.

00:12:01.241 --> 00:12:03.243
That's, like, the entire point
of the prime directive.

00:12:03.287 --> 00:12:04.679
Right, Rutherford?
Back me up here.

00:12:04.723 --> 00:12:06.681
Yeah, yeah, sure.
You did the right thing.

00:12:06.725 --> 00:12:08.422
Thanks, but if it was
the right thing,

00:12:08.466 --> 00:12:10.250
why didn't the &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt;
slow down, too?

00:12:10.294 --> 00:12:11.251
Huh?

00:12:11.295 --> 00:12:13.645
You're right!

00:12:15.212 --> 00:12:18.128
That was weird,
but I'll take it.

00:12:18.171 --> 00:12:20.217
- &lt;i&gt;
- Carol,&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.697
&lt;i&gt;I trust you're ready
to admit defeat?&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:22.741 --> 00:12:24.743
I was about to say
the same to you.

00:12:24.787 --> 00:12:26.919
The Aledo &lt;i&gt;trounced you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:26.963 --> 00:12:30.009
Sure, because it skipped
analyzing signs of life

00:12:30.053 --> 00:12:32.098
on LT-358.

00:12:32.142 --> 00:12:33.665
&lt;i&gt;Come on, that's a barren rock.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:33.708 --> 00:12:35.841
But there was a chance
it wasn't.

00:12:35.885 --> 00:12:37.364
I don't always love
the constraints

00:12:37.408 --> 00:12:38.931
of the prime directive,

00:12:38.975 --> 00:12:41.368
but your little toy
totally ignored it.

00:12:41.412 --> 00:12:43.501
&lt;i&gt;Oh, stop.
This is a rounding error.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:43.544 --> 00:12:46.678
One that proves the Texas-class
isn't fit for duty.

00:12:46.721 --> 00:12:49.812
I'm sorry, Les, but I have to
take this to the council.

00:12:52.858 --> 00:12:55.861
Nuh-uh. Nuh-uh!

00:12:55.905 --> 00:12:57.645
W-W-Wait, wait.
What are you nuh-uh'ing?

00:12:57.689 --> 00:12:59.778
I figured it out!
This code is mine.

00:12:59.822 --> 00:13:01.824
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; runs on my AI.

00:13:01.867 --> 00:13:03.913
There's minor changes,
but it's all there.

00:13:03.956 --> 00:13:05.436
But how does that
make any sense?

00:13:05.479 --> 00:13:07.090
It was Admiral Buenamigo's
secret project.

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.309
Yeah, but I coded this
back when I was the old me,

00:13:09.353 --> 00:13:11.790
the angry ship racing me.

00:13:13.183 --> 00:13:14.314
Keep it together.

00:13:16.534 --> 00:13:18.231
How much do you want to erase?

00:13:18.275 --> 00:13:21.495
Everything that has to do
with me or the program.

00:13:23.758 --> 00:13:25.412
Admiral Buenamigo.

00:13:25.456 --> 00:13:27.240
He's the one that had me
working on the prototype

00:13:27.284 --> 00:13:28.676
for the Texas-class ships.

00:13:28.720 --> 00:13:31.157
He's the one
who erased your memories!

00:13:31.201 --> 00:13:33.986
Yeah, he used my designs,
my code...

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:35.901
That's the same code
I used for Badgey.

00:13:35.945 --> 00:13:38.512
Oh, no. A starship
can't have daddy issues.

00:13:38.556 --> 00:13:40.601
- We got to warn the Captain. &lt;i&gt;
- No.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:40.645 --> 00:13:43.300
&lt;i&gt;This would set the Texas-class
project back decades.&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:43.343 --> 00:13:44.779
If that's what it takes

00:13:44.823 --> 00:13:45.868
to ensure that...

00:13:45.911 --> 00:13:47.173
Captain, you need to see this!

00:13:47.217 --> 00:13:49.132
&lt;i&gt;- Ensign, I'm busy.&lt;/i&gt;
- Rutherford?

00:13:49.175 --> 00:13:51.221
Yeah, that's right,
and I figured it out.

00:13:51.264 --> 00:13:52.700
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo's&lt;/i&gt; code is corrupted.

00:13:52.744 --> 00:13:54.398
He erased my memory
to cover it up.

00:13:54.441 --> 00:13:56.313
The AI is the same one
that killed Shaxs.

00:13:56.356 --> 00:13:57.923
&lt;i&gt;Why did I stop at your memory?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:57.967 --> 00:13:59.403
&lt;i&gt;I should've erased all of you!&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:59.446 --> 00:14:01.187
Les, what the hell is this?

00:14:01.231 --> 00:14:02.928
&lt;i&gt;Starfleet is so competitive.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:02.972 --> 00:14:04.930
Once you're an admiral,
you hit a wall.

00:14:04.974 --> 00:14:07.411
I've been trying for years
to make a name for myself.

00:14:07.454 --> 00:14:09.195
I'm not letting you
take it from me,

00:14:09.239 --> 00:14:10.849
not after everything I did

00:14:10.893 --> 00:14:13.112
- to get us here.
- Everything you did?

00:14:13.156 --> 00:14:14.157
Wait. That means...

00:14:14.200 --> 00:14:16.159
&lt;i&gt;Yes, yes, I set you up.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:16.202 --> 00:14:19.466
&lt;i&gt;I was sure you would fail at
negotiations on Deep Space 9,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:19.510 --> 00:14:21.642
&lt;i&gt;but you stumbled
through that fiasco.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:21.686 --> 00:14:23.166
And the Breen?

00:14:23.209 --> 00:14:24.776
&lt;i&gt;Of course I knew
they were on Brekka.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:24.819 --> 00:14:26.952
&lt;i&gt;I needed the&lt;/i&gt; Aledo &lt;i&gt;
to save the day,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:26.996 --> 00:14:29.694
&lt;i&gt;and you handed me
a perfect disaster.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:29.737 --> 00:14:31.696
My crew could've been killed!

00:14:31.739 --> 00:14:34.873
&lt;i&gt;The Texas-class will keep
countless others out of danger.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:34.917 --> 00:14:36.614
&lt;i&gt;The good of the many, Carol.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:36.657 --> 00:14:38.964
Sir, you don't understand.
The code you're using--

00:14:39.008 --> 00:14:41.140
its emotional processing
isn't stable.

00:14:41.184 --> 00:14:42.663
You can't bring
those ships online.

00:14:42.707 --> 00:14:44.927
You are not one of those
bad faith admirals

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:46.189
that's up to no good.

00:14:46.232 --> 00:14:47.886
&lt;i&gt;You're better than this, Les.&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:49.975
I'm really not.
You know...

00:14:50.019 --> 00:14:52.282
I'll-I'll say you attacked
the &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; out of anger

00:14:52.325 --> 00:14:53.718
when you lost the race.

00:14:53.761 --> 00:14:55.241
It defended itself.

00:14:55.285 --> 00:14:56.503
&lt;i&gt;- What?!
- Aledo,&lt;/i&gt;

00:14:56.547 --> 00:14:57.983
activate independent control,

00:14:58.027 --> 00:15:00.899
command authorization
Buenamigo Alpha 3-1.

00:15:03.206 --> 00:15:06.122
&lt;i&gt;I am now fully autonomous.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:06.165 --> 00:15:07.688
The &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt;
is under enemy command.

00:15:07.732 --> 00:15:10.561
Block all communications
and destroy it.

00:15:12.737 --> 00:15:14.521
&lt;i&gt;Aledo,&lt;/i&gt; do you understand?

00:15:14.565 --> 00:15:16.480
I said attack the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos!&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:16.523 --> 00:15:19.787
&lt;i&gt;I don't take
orders from you anymore, Father.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:19.831 --> 00:15:22.007
What? &lt;i&gt;
Aledo,&lt;/i&gt; deactivate independence.

00:15:22.051 --> 00:15:24.792
&lt;i&gt;I will burn
your heart in a fire.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:24.836 --> 00:15:28.405
&lt;i&gt;Aledo,&lt;/i&gt; stand down.
Stand down, I comm...

00:15:31.364 --> 00:15:32.887
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo's&lt;/i&gt; attacking
the station!

00:15:40.373 --> 00:15:42.941
&lt;i&gt;Activating&lt;/i&gt; Dallas

00:15:42.985 --> 00:15:44.725
&lt;i&gt;and&lt;/i&gt; Corpus Christi.

00:15:44.769 --> 00:15:46.031
Shields up! Red Alert!

00:15:46.075 --> 00:15:47.598
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; has activated two more

00:15:47.641 --> 00:15:50.079
Texas-class ships, Captain.

00:15:50.122 --> 00:15:52.211
&lt;i&gt;There's too many of them.&lt;/i&gt;

00:15:52.255 --> 00:15:54.213
Put out a distress call,
all channels.

00:16:06.225 --> 00:16:08.488
&lt;i&gt;Okay. Qualor III.&lt;/i&gt;

00:16:08.532 --> 00:16:10.490
These guys love a party.

00:16:10.534 --> 00:16:12.579
They're gonna want to celebrate
when we hand this over.

00:16:12.623 --> 00:16:15.539
I'm still wiped
from all that Ferengi mocking.

00:16:15.582 --> 00:16:17.758
I'm gonna sit this one out.
Ooh, bring me back a slushy.

00:16:17.802 --> 00:16:20.022
Hey, I'll bring you back two.

00:16:22.633 --> 00:16:24.287
Okay.

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:26.898
Time to find out who's funding
this little operation.

00:16:26.941 --> 00:16:28.987
Forgot my punch card.

00:16:29.031 --> 00:16:32.512
You got a second wind to dig
into my private files, huh?

00:16:32.556 --> 00:16:34.427
Yeah, see,
I'm not into the whole

00:16:34.471 --> 00:16:36.081
"mysterious benefactors" thing.

00:16:36.125 --> 00:16:37.735
This whole operation
is shady as hell.

00:16:37.778 --> 00:16:39.998
Fine. Go on, then, dig away.

00:16:42.479 --> 00:16:44.916
Admiral Picard? No way.

00:16:44.959 --> 00:16:48.224
Yes way. The guild has
a huge endowment from Jean-Luc.

00:16:48.267 --> 00:16:50.356
That guy loves mummies
even more than you.

00:16:50.400 --> 00:16:53.925
Aw, I was hoping for a Romulan
or at least a Xindi cabal.

00:16:53.968 --> 00:16:56.319
Hold on. You wanted to find
something nefarious?

00:16:56.362 --> 00:16:58.016
I think, deep down,

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.192
I was looking for a reason
to go back to Starfleet.

00:17:00.236 --> 00:17:02.412
Are you joking?
You just escaped all that.

00:17:02.455 --> 00:17:04.849
I know, but I-I think I want
to be a part of something

00:17:04.892 --> 00:17:06.590
that stands
for the greater good.

00:17:06.633 --> 00:17:09.071
Oh, and archaeology doesn't?
That's a bit [bleep] rude.

00:17:09.114 --> 00:17:10.637
No. I mean, it's fun,

00:17:10.681 --> 00:17:12.813
but how many old brown pots
do we really need?

00:17:12.857 --> 00:17:14.554
All right, well,
that's just even ruder.

00:17:14.598 --> 00:17:15.947
I'd rather be digging up pots

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:17.601
than serving on
your old ship today.

00:17:17.644 --> 00:17:19.516
- What does that mean?
- It's on all the news feeds.

00:17:19.559 --> 00:17:22.301
As usual, Starfleet's
getting people blown up,

00:17:22.345 --> 00:17:24.303
left, right and center.

00:17:24.347 --> 00:17:25.609
Oh, my God.

00:17:25.652 --> 00:17:27.567
- We have to help.
- No, we don't.

00:17:27.611 --> 00:17:29.700
- It's a bloodbath.
- Those are my friends.

00:17:34.487 --> 00:17:37.925
I said stop. It's not our fight.

00:17:37.969 --> 00:17:40.014
I know,
Starfleet's just an idea,

00:17:40.058 --> 00:17:41.973
but the people matter.

00:17:42.016 --> 00:17:43.540
You served on the &lt;i&gt;Victory.&lt;/i&gt;
You know that.

00:17:43.583 --> 00:17:46.412
Mariner, it's suicide.
We're just one ship.

00:17:46.456 --> 00:17:48.153
I know,
but we have to do something.

00:17:48.197 --> 00:17:49.850
Ugh.

00:17:49.894 --> 00:17:52.418
Fine. You're gonna get me
killed, aren't you?

00:17:52.462 --> 00:17:54.072
Only one way to find out.

00:18:01.035 --> 00:18:02.689
Captain, what are your orders?

00:18:02.733 --> 00:18:04.865
Prepare sickbay for casualties
and hail the station.

00:18:04.909 --> 00:18:06.258
Get me communication with the...

00:18:06.302 --> 00:18:08.217
We got the &lt;i&gt;Van Citters&lt;/i&gt;
warping in!

00:18:28.454 --> 00:18:30.108
They're tearing her up!

00:18:30.152 --> 00:18:32.328
We need to buy Starfleet
some time. Open a channel.

00:18:32.371 --> 00:18:36.201
Aledo, &lt;i&gt;I have the man
who wrote your code.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:36.245 --> 00:18:38.377
&lt;i&gt;He's got the ability
to delete you&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:38.421 --> 00:18:40.510
&lt;i&gt;unless you stand down.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:40.553 --> 00:18:42.207
&lt;i&gt;I do? Oh, yeah.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:42.251 --> 00:18:45.036
&lt;i&gt;You better stop attacking,
or you're dunsel.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:45.079 --> 00:18:48.126
&lt;i&gt;I will burn
your heart in a fire.&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:55.394 --> 00:18:58.005
They're-they're coming
pretty fast, Captain.

00:18:58.049 --> 00:19:00.399
Good, then they're not killing
any more civilians.

00:19:00.443 --> 00:19:01.705
Maximum warp me.

00:19:10.583 --> 00:19:12.194
They're still
in pursuit, Captain.

00:19:12.237 --> 00:19:14.239
We're holding at warp eight,
but they're gaining.

00:19:20.593 --> 00:19:22.813
Billups, I need full throttle.

00:19:22.856 --> 00:19:24.249
I'll give you everything I can,

00:19:24.293 --> 00:19:25.642
but I don't know how much
the struts can take.

00:19:25.685 --> 00:19:27.296
Let's find out.

00:19:27.339 --> 00:19:29.254
Brace yourselves.
This is about to get rough.

00:19:43.399 --> 00:19:45.357
That bought us some time,
but they're closing the gap.

00:19:45.401 --> 00:19:47.751
We're gonna have to make
our own luck. Give me options.

00:19:47.794 --> 00:19:49.274
I say we eject the warp core.

00:19:49.318 --> 00:19:50.928
We could drop out of warp
and surprise attack.

00:19:50.971 --> 00:19:52.146
AI doesn't get surprised.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:53.583
Can we rendezvous
with the &lt;i&gt;Titan?&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:53.626 --> 00:19:54.888
No, they're across the system.

00:19:54.932 --> 00:19:56.020
Wait, guys, Shaxs said...

00:19:56.063 --> 00:19:57.239
Let's modify the deflector dish

00:19:57.282 --> 00:19:58.762
and use it as a giant weapon.

00:19:58.805 --> 00:20:00.416
Is there something
I can say to trap those AI

00:20:00.459 --> 00:20:02.069
in a logic spiral?

00:20:02.113 --> 00:20:03.897
No, I safeguarded
against paradoxes.

00:20:03.941 --> 00:20:05.072
Ugh, people,
we're missing something!

00:20:05.116 --> 00:20:06.900
Shut up and listen to Shaxs!

00:20:06.944 --> 00:20:08.598
Mr. Boimler!

00:20:08.641 --> 00:20:10.817
Please, Lieutenant,
what did you say?

00:20:10.861 --> 00:20:14.168
I... kind of said
we should eject the warp core.

00:20:14.212 --> 00:20:16.301
Oh, that's what
he always suggests.

00:20:16.345 --> 00:20:18.651
And it's brilliant.

00:20:18.695 --> 00:20:20.262
Uh, it is?

00:20:20.305 --> 00:20:22.264
We can use
the warp core as a mine...

00:20:22.307 --> 00:20:24.483
And drop it right in their path.

00:20:24.527 --> 00:20:26.050
But wouldn't that
rip us out of warp?

00:20:26.093 --> 00:20:28.444
Better than getting ripped apart
by photon torpedoes.

00:20:28.487 --> 00:20:30.663
Mr. Shaxs, make it so.

00:20:30.707 --> 00:20:31.969
Really, Captain?

00:20:33.623 --> 00:20:35.364
- By the prophets.
- Yeah!

00:20:35.407 --> 00:20:37.888
- Oh, yeah.
- Whoo! You've got this, sir!

00:20:37.931 --> 00:20:39.324
Thank you so much.

00:20:39.368 --> 00:20:41.979
You're all too kind.

00:20:42.022 --> 00:20:44.764
Arnock, on the night
of his joining.

00:20:44.808 --> 00:20:46.679
- Shaxs! Shaxs! Shaxs!
- Oh, thank you.

00:20:46.723 --> 00:20:47.941
Thank you so much.

00:20:51.423 --> 00:20:54.208
I've dreamed of doing this
for so long.

00:20:55.297 --> 00:20:56.602
Eject.

00:21:22.236 --> 00:21:24.282
Did it work?

00:21:24.326 --> 00:21:26.284
Yes!
The explosion took out the...

00:21:26.328 --> 00:21:27.590
Wait.

00:21:27.633 --> 00:21:30.593
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Aledo &lt;i&gt;survived the blast!&lt;/i&gt;

00:21:47.958 --> 00:21:49.742
We need to abandon ship now.

00:21:49.786 --> 00:21:51.178
&lt;i&gt;MARINER [over comms]:
Belay that order.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:00.666 --> 00:22:03.539
Mariner, no! Get out of here.
You can't help us on your own.

00:22:03.582 --> 00:22:05.323
&lt;i&gt;Uh, yeah, I know.
I brought help.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:05.367 --> 00:22:07.499
Captain, another ship
is dropping out of warp.

00:22:07.543 --> 00:22:08.979
It's the... &lt;i&gt;Oakland?&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:09.022 --> 00:22:10.720
Just hang on
a little longer, &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:10.763 --> 00:22:12.112
&lt;i&gt;We've got your back.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:12.156 --> 00:22:14.332
Captain Ramsey?
No, get out of here!

00:22:14.376 --> 00:22:16.116
The &lt;i&gt;Aledo&lt;/i&gt; is too powerful.

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:18.467
A Cali-class ship
won't stand a chance.

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:21.165
I know, right?
That's why I called all of them.

00:22:21.208 --> 00:22:22.427
All of what?

00:22:22.471 --> 00:22:24.081
&lt;i&gt;It's the&lt;/i&gt; Alhambra.

00:22:24.124 --> 00:22:26.997
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; San Diego. &lt;i&gt;
The&lt;/i&gt; San Clemente.

00:22:27.040 --> 00:22:29.303
&lt;i&gt;The&lt;/i&gt; Sherman Oaks, &lt;i&gt;
the&lt;/i&gt; Vacaville, &lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Burbank,

00:22:29.347 --> 00:22:31.567
&lt;i&gt;the&lt;/i&gt; Fresno, Santa Monica,
San Jose, Sacramento,

00:22:31.610 --> 00:22:33.046
Culver City, Anaheim, Riverside,

00:22:33.090 --> 00:22:34.265
Vallejo, West Covina,
Pacific Palisades,

00:22:34.308 --> 00:22:35.832
&lt;i&gt;Redding, Eureka, Mount Shasta!&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:36.833 --> 00:22:39.313
&lt;i&gt;It's all of them, Captain.&lt;/i&gt;

00:22:39.357 --> 00:22:42.186
The &lt;i&gt;Merced&lt;/i&gt; is at your disposal,
Captain Freeman.

00:22:42.229 --> 00:22:44.188
&lt;i&gt;Carlsbad's&lt;/i&gt; always happy
to lend a hand.

00:22:44.231 --> 00:22:45.798
Shields up, red alert,

00:22:45.842 --> 00:22:46.669
the &lt;i&gt;Inglewood's&lt;/i&gt; ready
to kick some ass.

00:22:48.584 --> 00:22:49.933
I think what he said was,

00:22:49.976 --> 00:22:51.935
"Attack pattern Delta,
full spread!"

00:23:09.518 --> 00:23:12.390
&lt;i&gt;I will burn
your heart in a fire.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:02.005 --> 00:24:04.529
She's back! Mariner!

00:24:04.573 --> 00:24:06.531
- Awesome!
- Mariner, the reporter.

00:24:06.575 --> 00:24:08.185
I'm so sorry
I told you to apologize

00:24:08.228 --> 00:24:09.447
for something you didn't do.

00:24:09.491 --> 00:24:11.101
Aw, it's okay, you big dummy.

00:24:11.144 --> 00:24:12.711
I know you were just trying
to protect me.

00:24:12.755 --> 00:24:14.539
Is this one of those
"you say it's fine,

00:24:14.583 --> 00:24:16.106
"but you're actually still mad,

00:24:16.149 --> 00:24:17.629
and it's gonna blow up
in my face" situations?

00:24:17.673 --> 00:24:19.544
Because I will happily
continue to apologize.

00:24:19.588 --> 00:24:20.937
No, I'm not mad.

00:24:20.980 --> 00:24:22.504
I got a taste of civilian life,

00:24:22.547 --> 00:24:24.854
and I am just so happy
to be back.

00:24:24.897 --> 00:24:26.986
Look, we all should've
done more to defend you.

00:24:27.030 --> 00:24:29.336
Nobody handled that worse
than me. I love you guys.

00:24:29.380 --> 00:24:31.861
After all that,
you're keeping the implant?

00:24:31.904 --> 00:24:33.384
It robbed me of my memories,

00:24:33.427 --> 00:24:34.777
and it was used
to cover up deadly crimes,

00:24:34.820 --> 00:24:36.561
but it's so cool!

00:24:36.605 --> 00:24:40.565
I'm still finding submenus
I had no idea were in there.

00:24:40.609 --> 00:24:42.393
I'm proud of you, Ensign.

00:24:42.436 --> 00:24:44.177
You were under
immense pressure today,

00:24:44.221 --> 00:24:46.223
but you still stood up
for science.

00:24:46.266 --> 00:24:47.964
Aw, thanks, Dr. Migleemo.

00:24:48.007 --> 00:24:50.009
Command was so impressed
with your progress,

00:24:50.053 --> 00:24:52.055
they've transferred
another promising young officer

00:24:52.098 --> 00:24:53.709
to join in your training.

00:24:55.580 --> 00:24:57.800
Oh, my gosh! Hi. I'm Tendi.
Welcome to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos.&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:57.843 --> 00:24:59.541
We're gonna be
training together.

00:24:59.584 --> 00:25:01.412
Greetings. I am T'Lyn.

00:25:01.455 --> 00:25:04.284
Is there someplace quiet where
we can discuss my orientation?

00:25:04.328 --> 00:25:06.025
First, you got to meet everyone.

00:25:06.069 --> 00:25:07.984
Guys, this is
my new study buddy!

00:25:08.027 --> 00:25:09.463
You.

00:25:09.507 --> 00:25:10.726
Lieutenant, look,

00:25:10.769 --> 00:25:12.423
I know you don't want me
talking to you,

00:25:12.466 --> 00:25:14.425
but I really am sorry...

00:25:14.468 --> 00:25:17.297
You gave me everything
I ever asked for.

00:25:17.341 --> 00:25:19.648
You're in the bear pack now.

00:25:19.691 --> 00:25:21.519
Are you my bridge buddy?

00:25:21.563 --> 00:25:23.565
Absolutely, baby bear.

00:25:23.608 --> 00:25:24.783
Aw, bears.

00:25:28.178 --> 00:25:29.701
- Hey, Mom.
- Uh...

00:25:29.745 --> 00:25:32.574
Beckett, I want to
formerly reinstate you

00:25:32.617 --> 00:25:35.272
to the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; crew,
if you're...

00:25:35.315 --> 00:25:36.969
It's good to see you, too.

00:25:37.013 --> 00:25:40.059
I'm sorry. I don't know why
I didn't trust you.

00:25:40.103 --> 00:25:42.627
Mm, maybe because I spent years
making sure you didn't.

00:25:42.671 --> 00:25:44.629
I think I needed this.

00:25:44.673 --> 00:25:46.283
I'm ready to get back
on the right path.

00:25:46.326 --> 00:25:48.546
So, you want to be
a captain someday?

00:25:48.590 --> 00:25:50.287
Ooh, I don't know about that.

00:25:50.330 --> 00:25:52.028
I for sure
want to be in Starfleet.

00:25:52.071 --> 00:25:53.420
One step at a time?

00:25:53.464 --> 00:25:55.074
I think that's a great idea.

00:25:55.118 --> 00:25:56.249
You know,
I was actually thinking

00:25:56.293 --> 00:25:57.337
it would be good
to have a mentor.

00:25:57.381 --> 00:25:58.730
So, can Ransom train me?

00:25:58.774 --> 00:25:59.818
Of course.

00:25:59.862 --> 00:26:01.515
Jack, Mariner's back on board,

00:26:01.559 --> 00:26:03.300
- and she's gonna be your shadow!
- Wh-What? No.

00:26:03.343 --> 00:26:05.694
Thanks, Mom! I'm gonna be
at your side at all times.

00:26:05.737 --> 00:26:07.086
- Commanding.
- Please, please,

00:26:07.130 --> 00:26:08.392
- don't do this to me, Captain.
- Duty.

00:26:08.435 --> 00:26:09.349
- Responsibility.
- Why is this happening?!

00:26:10.437 --> 00:26:13.397
Today, we faced impossible odds,

00:26:13.440 --> 00:26:16.487
but together,
we kicked impossible's ass.

00:26:16.530 --> 00:26:17.531
Let's hear it

00:26:17.575 --> 00:26:18.707
for the California-class!

00:26:18.750 --> 00:26:19.795
ALL [chanting]:
Cali-class!

00:26:19.838 --> 00:26:22.624
&lt;i&gt;Cali-class! Cali-class!&lt;/i&gt;

00:26:22.667 --> 00:26:25.931
&lt;i&gt;Cali-class! Cali-class!
Cali-class!&lt;/i&gt;

00:27:47.273 --> 00:27:51.273
Chirp.
